## native/core/crates/mixdog-js/src/locale_compare.rs (lead/UTF16-owner integration)

There must be ONE OS default-locale reader. In collator(), replace the existing
sys_locale::get_locale conversion with:

    let locale = crate::default_locale::default_locale_tag()
        .parse::<Locale>()
        .unwrap_or(Locale::UNKNOWN);

Remove this module's old `pub fn default_locale_tag() -> String` implementation.
If local callers/tests need that name in scope, import the shared helper:

    use crate::default_locale::default_locale_tag;

Do not retain UI-preference-based reading alongside the new regional-locale path.
Exact new helper signatures:

    pub fn default_locale_id() -> &'static str;
    pub fn default_locale_tag() -> String;

The ID is the once-cached ICU-style OS default. The tag uses V8's POSIX fallback
mapping (en_US_POSIX -> en-US), ICU's ISO3/region/deprecated-tag maps, variants, legacy tags and Unicode
keyword/type mappings (including numbering and collation extensions).
Windows uses GetLocaleInfoEx(USER_DEFAULT, LOCALE_SNAME), not preferred UI languages.
Unix/macOS query setlocale(LC_MESSAGES, null) read-only, then ICU's LC_ALL,
LC_MESSAGES, LANG fallback order. LANGUAGE is not consulted; setlocale is never
called with an empty string or another mutating locale argument.

