## Implementation and source contract

Pinned official Node v22.20.0 archive:
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nodejs/node/v22.20.0/deps/icu-small/source/data/in/icudt77l.dat.bz2
SHA256 488a0a666ba33dace736d0788a8973729c8d83f3f4966d0fed1be7ad162d4729.
The archive itself reports ICU77.1/CLDR47/tz2025b. The independent Python binary
resource reader handles pooled keys/strings and ICU resource types directly;
it does not use the installed ICU72 data or algorithms to extract the dataset.
Official resource-parser contracts are ICU77 uresdata.h/cpp and uresbund.cpp.
Original source contracts and Unicode/V8 licenses are preserved in the fixture's
reference directory and SHA256-indexed by date_string/data/PROVENANCE.json.

Runtime data: 526 locale resources (including root; tzdbNames is not a locale),
936 numbering locale resources, 639 timezone IDs/links, canonical CLDR aliases,
long standard/daylight names, all locale parent/alias chains, current-time
metazone periods, localized GMT formats/digits, ICU raw/DST transition pairs and
final recurring rules. No fixture-locale hardcoding or English-only fallback.

Production payload:
- date_string/data/icu77-date-names.json.gz: 371,010 bytes; expands to 2,299,937 bytes.
  SHA256 c4c8697b5b518aad8a52a74a487b92396cc02a00ba66d7720c583e4371422106.
- default_locale/data/icu77-locale.json: 57,361 bytes.
  SHA256 0873cdb1db2a6e0ecd5b999c3328eea923248098d912e59549109a21a9a627d6.
Only this compact data is included in the runtime; the 11.1MB source archive and
source/license provenance are development artifacts, not a runtime Node dependency.

V8 chooses the DST name after EquivalentTime for dates outside the signed-32-bit
nonnegative epoch; ICU display-name lookup uses the current clock for metazones
and fallback raw/DST savings, not the Date's year. Negative-DST zones use ICU's
raw/DST decomposition, not chrono-tz's different Ireland/Morocco decomposition.
Names are cached by zone, locale and daylight flag. The prefix keeps V8's English
weekday/month tokens, offset formatting and negative-year minimum width (-0001).

The pinned ICU transitions also provide consistent numeric offsets when the
shared chrono helpers stop at their year/final-transition horizon. Within matching
chrono fields/offsets, the existing time helpers are reused. No shared Date
arithmetic/parser behaviour was changed: their chrono extreme-year limitations
and the existing process_zone/Tz restriction on custom/unknown TZ IDs remain
separate shared-time follow-ups. This change must not be described as fixing all
Date arithmetic or arbitrary POSIX/custom TZ environment syntax.

