The actual installed Node22.20/V8 12.4/ICU77.1/tz2025b default locale was ko-KR.
Corpus: 3,981 direct Date.toString calls over all 639 IDs, epoch/pre-epoch,
historical/DST/boundary/equivalent years, invalid dates and the full JS time range;
4,761 direct Node Intl long-name probes over supported locales, stable current
metazones and fixed-offset GMT fallbacks (including numbering extensions).
Root is not a valid Intl locale tag and is explicitly listed as such; root resource
fallback remains in the complete dataset. No returned-value mismatch is skipped.
The locale-name probes intentionally use stable current metazones so Intl's
input-date naming is not substituted for DateCache's current-time naming contract.

Source/data-level diagnostics reproduced every recorded date and name using the
extracted data (0 differences). This is NOT a Rust compile or Rust test pass.
After applying the fragment, root must run offline mixdog-js tests for date_string
and default_locale, existing locale_compare tests, and the affected formula twins;
then clippy/all-targets. This worker ran rustfmt parsing, extraction, bounded Node
recording and source checks only. No Cargo/build/apps/profiles/commit was run.

## Why system ICU was not used

The installed Windows ICU is72.1/tz2022g; its America/Coyhaique display name is GMT,
while the pinned Node2025b answers GMT-03:00. Windows/Linux/macOS system data versions
cannot promise pinned parity. Cached chrono/jiff supply no localized CLDR names;
icu_datetime is not cached. No new crate/package was downloaded or installed.

Golden SHA256: 58669326e3f9c332033784b6c3041737e19f30acea85165f88bdf4afa2ae561c.
Total embedded payload is 428,371 bytes before linker/compressor overhead.
The redistribution package must retain the Unicode/ICU and V8 third-party notices.
POSIX/macOS locale selection is source-ported but was not executed on this Windows
worker; root must retain the platform verification gate rather than asserting a
measured pass for those native locale entry points.
